The point about gismu is debatable, and on balance I feel it's untrue. But
nothing precludes uncountable sumti places in general, so a debate about
gismu places isn't really necessary here.

On 17 Oct 2011 03:53, "John E Clifford" <kali9putra@yahoo.com> wrote:

On countables.  Remember that Lojban has no mass gismu, all are count.
 Whether
we can eventually get a mass noun as a derived form is terribly not clear
(largely because it is unclear what the various words that look to be about
masses really mean).

Segments are more obscure than types -- and conversely; let's stick to
things
until someone can demonstrate an actual need for something else.  I haven't
seen
it yet.




